  "bio": [
    "Arvid Lunnemark cofounded Cursor, the maker of a popular AI code editing tool, with three friends from MIT in 2022.",
    "The company was acquired by SpaceX for $60 billion in August 2026. Forbes estimates that each Cursor cofounder received shares of the rocket maker worth $2.4 billion at the deal's closing.",
    "Before the SpaceX acquisition, Cursor claimed to have more than $1 billion in annualized revenue, making it one of the fastest growing AI startups.",
    "Today, millions of software developers at enterprises like Nvidia, Adobe, Uber and Shopify use Cursor to generate and edit chunks of code.",
    "Originally from Sweden, Lunnemark left Cursor in 2025 to launch a new startup called Integrous Research, which is focused on developing systems for safer AI.",
    "A former math olympiad champion, Lunnemark did internships in quantitative trading at Jane Street and software engineering at Stripe before cofounding Cursor."
